{
  "_comment": [
    "Every scripted capture the area list shows and the box simulator counts:",
    "the starter, gifts, trades, statics, fossils and eggs (Ian, 2026-09-26).",
    "Species and levels come from docs/oxide/pokemon-sources.csv, matched by",
    "`from` (the script or trade file, and a level when one file holds two",
    "sources); `pool` names them outright where there is no row to match.",
    "`capture_area` is the location name the Pokemon's met location takes,",
    "so a source that shares a name with a wild table is an alternative to",
    "it (scripted-sources.md, 'Captures before the League'). An egg counts",
    "where it hatches, which the player picks, so it has no capture area of",
    "its own. `order` places a source with a location of its own in play",
    "order; one that shares a table's location takes that table's order.",
    "`pick` is how the player ends up with one member of the pool: random",
    "(even odds), choice, or legendary_pool (the lake caverns draw without",
    "replacement from the availability plan's pool). `simulate: false` keeps",
    "a source out of the box simulator. Left out on purpose: the roamers",
    "(they take the name of the route they are caught on), the Great Marsh",
    "and Trophy Garden dailies, the Unown rooms, and the event legendaries."
  ],
